The height after \( d \) days is \( 4 \times 2^d \).
We want this height to be greater than 20 feet:
\[ 4 \times 2^d > 20 \]
Divide both sides by 4:
\[ 2^d > 5 \]
Take the logarithm of both sides:
\[ \log(2^d) > \log(5) \]
\[ d > \log(5) \]
Calculate \( \log(5) \):
\[ \log(5) \approx 1.608 \]
Since \( d \) must be an integer, we round up to the next whole number:
\[ d = 2 \]
